@startuml use-cases
left to right direction

actor Organizer

rectangle Pachanguero {
  usecase "UC-001-01\nCreate a season with\nno roster re-entry" as UC01
  usecase "UC-001-02\nCapture seniority on\nfirst appearance" as UC02
  usecase "UC-001-08\nResolve which game a\ncandidate paste targets" as UC08
  usecase "UC-001-03\nPaste & resolve the\nSunday candidate list" as UC03
  usecase "UC-001-04\nRegister a new player\ninline" as UC04
  usecase "UC-001-09\nMaintain a player's\nnicknames/aliases" as UC09
  usecase "UC-001-05\nRun the algorithmic\nConvocatoria" as UC05
  usecase "UC-001-10\nResolve which game a\nfinal-list paste targets" as UC10
  usecase "UC-001-06\nPaste & resolve the\nfinal Claros/Oscuros list" as UC06
  usecase "UC-001-07\nBackfill a historical\ngame (final list only)" as UC07
}

Organizer --> UC01
Organizer --> UC03
Organizer --> UC05
Organizer --> UC06
Organizer --> UC07

UC03 ..> UC08 : <<include>>
UC06 ..> UC10 : <<include>>

UC03 ..> UC04 : <<include>>
UC06 ..> UC04 : <<include>>

UC03 ..> UC09 : <<include>>
UC06 ..> UC09 : <<include>>

UC03 ..> UC02 : <<include>>
UC06 ..> UC02 : <<include>>

UC03 .[#gray].> UC05 : <<precedes>>
UC05 .[#gray].> UC06 : <<precedes>>

UC07 ..> UC06 : <<extend>>
UC07 ..> UC10 : <<extend>>
note right of UC07
  reuses UC-001-06's resolution and
  finalization behaviour, and UC-001-10's
  explicit-override path (S3), skipping
  UC-001-03 / UC-001-08 / UC-001-05
end note

@enduml
